   "file": "TauCeti/Computability/SacksSplitting/Routing.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp] step_fst : (step r A D).1 = A.1 \u222a routedBatch r (D \\ (A.1 \u222a A.2)) false` and the matching `step_snd`. Also add `mem_step_fst_iff : x \u2208 (step r A D).1 \u2194 x \u2208 A.1 \u2228 (x \u2208 D \u2227 x \u2209 A.1 \u222a A.2 \u2227 route r x = false)` and its `snd`/`true` counterpart. Then rewrite the injury-attribution proof to use these lemmas instead of `simp only [step]`.",
   "issue": "`step` has only the pair equation `step_def` (not simp). There are no `@[simp]` component lemmas and no `mem_*_iff` lemmas. As a result, `exists_higher_priority_of_mem_injuriesAt` unfolds the definition with `simp only [step] at hfirst hsecond`, and the monotonicity proofs go through `congrArg Prod.fst`/`Prod.snd`.",
